        "id": 132719,
        "name": "Rabk",
        "username": "Rabk",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabk/{size}/1978_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-21T02:56:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Think about it thematically: When Miss Information flips, she becomes a target. Her card was already in play, but it was only when her secret identity is revealed that Expatriette has something to shoot at. If the <em>target</em> did not enter play Hairtrigger Reflexes could not react to her unveiling and Expat would just sit there helplessly while the erstwhile secretary laughed in her face. The same applies to Imbued Vitality. Ongoings are normally just static effects that require massive RPG-style intervention for Expat to handle. When that Reactive Playing she’s been dancing around suddenly comes to life, however, you bet your ass that she can recognize a puny 6hp target when she sees it, and come out with guns blazing.</p>\n<p>Was there a target in play before? (No.) Is there a target now? (Yes.) Did a target therefore enter play? (Yes, indeed.)</p>",
        "post_number": 23,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:08:14.960Z",
